program	consumes_foreign_module_declaration_error.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	`leak` cannot be declared `consumes` here: a consuming method replaces `Handle`'s teardown, and this module does not define `Handle`
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: `leak` cannot be declared `consumes` here: a consuming method replaces `Handle`'s teardown, and this module does not define `Handle`"
log	"  --> examples/consumes_foreign_module_declaration_error.saw:26:5"
log	"     |"
log	" 26 |     func leak(&var self) consumes {}"
log	"     |     ^"
log	"   hint: declare it in `consumes260` (which defines `Handle`) — overriding a type's teardown is the type author's privilege, the same containment its `deinit` has. From here, take the value by value in a free function instead (`consume(move obj)`)"
log	""
log	"1 error(s) generated"
